+# PF7-sub62 shield.cash reparameterization - measured research report
+
+Status: qualified research only. Not a maintainer-bench submission, Chipnet
+broadcast, deployment bundle, ceremony result, or release claim.
+
+## Locked route and authority
+
+`bn254-onetx-pf7-sub62-r1` was preserved: PairFold topology 7 (five
+executors, genesis, terminal), KWIN 13, five striped fragments, static
+gamma/delta table, composed P2SH, scalar endpoint, self-carried terminal, and
+fixed witness-table allocation `0,1536,2460,2427,2304`. No repartitioning,
+density padding, or generic adapter route was used.
+
+Candidate manifest SHA-256:
+`c03e8ae157998f513f058433e58e3252e05a2d2c39f5577a992d39c9daf3ff19`.
+
+The only variable material was the complete, SHA-256-pinned shield adapter. In
+adapter mode `_millermath.mjs` sets `committedVec` to `undefined`, validates
+the adapter's Groth16 pairing equation, and exports the adapter VK, proof, and
+public inputs. `fixed-g2-lines.mjs` gets `trajectory()/stepFactorSpec()` from
+the live `vk.gamma` and `vk.delta`; its fixed line table therefore regenerates
+at the adapter boundary and holds no selected shield v0 VK/proof constants.
+
+Source SHA-256: `_millermath.mjs`
+`60c6a13d1d9a60fb670475e9ae59965b060a817125d70ffead9751d8ad0c99c4`;
+`fixed-g2-lines.mjs`
+`e14fbc19ee29c8a0014f276c1e61176d0c42121d1e5809a9dbdc3b650db90dae`.
+
