+The same verifier-set SHA-256 across actions proves lock invariance for
+deposit, transfer, and withdrawal within each setup. The v0 and v1 hashes
+differ, as required for a setup replacement.
+
+## Adversarial and validation results
+
+`measure-terminal-raw-attacks.ts` now discovers the terminal and tests only
+the verifier prefix, so it applies to exact seven-role PF7 rather than assuming
+the obsolete ten-role layout. Both v0-deposit and v1-deposit reports had honest
+`allAccept=true`, then rejected all 18 mutations: seven lock-byte changes,
+seven adjacent role-witness substitutions, source-lock permutation, witness
+permutation, carrier length, and carrier byte. False accepts: 0; setup errors: 0.
+
+Raw-attack SHA-256: v0
+`c7f006e0dc40ee2fe1f7a74caf544fa554b513d74c9f4279d0c1da9fc83fd9ca`;
+v1 `6f5a325fd3a9b15af1b6ed4f6f257b92a634e9274caed869eaf585482895b0f3`.
+
+Reproduction after the exact PF7-sub62 build:
+
+```sh
+harness/node_modules/.bin/tsx lanes/bn254-onetx/src/c7/build.ts
+harness/node_modules/.bin/tsx lanes/bn254-onetx/src/c7/check-standardness.ts "$C7_TMP" "$C7_TMP/standardness.json"
+harness/node_modules/.bin/tsx lanes/bn254-onetx/src/c7/measure-terminal-raw-attacks.ts "$C7_TMP" "$C7_TMP/raw-attacks.json"
+```
+
+`node --test lanes/bn254-onetx/test/shield-adapter-input.test.mjs` passed 4/4.
+`npm test` is unavailable because this worktree has no `test` package script;
+the condition was observed before and after the changes.
+
+## Verdict
+
+PASS for the stated research gate: exact PF7-sub62 topology, six real
+development-only proof replays, wire <=54,739, every unlock <10,000, real
+BCH-2026 consensus VM acceptance, and real standard-VM acceptance. This does
+not establish maintainer-bench compatibility, Chipnet relay, funding,
+broadcast, ceremony quality, or production readiness.
